          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Netanyahu announces specific election month preference publicly</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 30-90 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 Days</div>

      <!-- N3: Hormuz July 31 (61 days remaining) -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N3 · 2026-05-31-hormuz-50-transits-by-july-31</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will at least 50 commercial vessels per day transit the Strait of Hormuz (&#8805;40–50% of pre-war ~120/day baseline) during any consecutive 7-day window before EOD 2026-07-31?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">28%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New · initial assignment</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">&#8594; resolves by 2026-07-31</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Initial assignment replacing F1 with extended 61-day horizon. Current transit data: ~4–24 vessels/day (4–20% of baseline) as of May 24–30. ADNOC CEO Sultan Al Jaber: "at least 4 months to reach 80% of pre-conflict flows, full flows not before Q1-Q2 2027." Path to 50/day by July 31 requires: (1) MOU signed in June (~35% per N1); (2) mine removal begins under 30-day MOU clause; (3) Lloyd's premiums fall below 1.5% hull value; (4) major shipping lines announce return. At ~2 months from today, ADNOC's 4-month minimum makes even 50/day (40–50% of baseline) a below-50% outcome. The 61-day window provides meaningful room over F1 but multiple sequential conditions must resolve favorably.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if IMF PortWatch, Hormuz Strait Monitor, UNCTAD, Lloyd's List, or Windward report &#8805;50 daily transits averaged over 7 consecutive days within any window ending before EOD 2026-07-31. Third-country vessels count ONLY IF &#8805;2 sources confirm independence from IRGC-linked tolls.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Minimum two independent confirming sources. If &#8805;2 sources cannot confirm within 30 days post-horizon: AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Dark-fleet or IRGC-toll vessels without independent Western confirmation = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Western insurer refusal persists at horizon = NOT sufficient for YES. PGSA self-reported figures excluded by default.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">US-Iran MOU signed — mine-removal clock starts</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Lloyd's premium below 1.5% hull value (sustained 7-day basis)</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Maersk/MSC/Frontline announce return to Hormuz routing</span>
        </div>
      </div>

